    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** enter today's slate leaning heavily on **Kyle Tucker** (80.25) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.27), who stand as our premier anchors. **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against Singer; the combination of a favorable park factor and a solid platoon advantage against a right-handed arm makes him an elite play. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** is positioned for a high-output night. His 75.27 score is heavily influenced by a massive +14% park boost and a +13% platoon edge against Gordon, making him our most impactful hitter relative to base projections. **Miguel Vargas** also earns a strong recommendation (59.81) against Valdez; notably, his score is bolstered by a +2% bump for facing a slow-delivery pitcher, which increases the likelihood of a stolen base\u2014a critical metric for our scarcity-focused strategy.\n\nRegarding bench decisions, the most difficult choice centered on the lower-ceiling utility options. **Wade Meckler** (45.19) just squeezed into the lineup over reserve candidates due to his favorable #3 spot in the order and a +7% platoon advantage against Bradley. While the overall score remains in the \"marginal\" tier, his ability to provide consistent at-bats kept him ahead of other bench depth. We are currently navigating a quiet day for our power-hitting core; **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** are completely sidelined today, while the active roster continues to manage around the persistent IL absences of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Andy Pages**. We are monitoring **Liam Hicks** (43.93) closely; while he projects as a starter, the combination of a high-xERA opponent in Springs and an unfavorable platoon split means his margin for error is slim. There are no immediate weather threats, but owners should keep an eye on lineup fluidity, as any movement down the batting order for **Liam Hicks** or **Wade Meckler** could push them below our daily efficiency threshold.",
